  journal   = "American Economic Review",
  publisher = "American Economic Association",
  volume    =  115,
  number    =  4,
  pages     = "1301--1337",
  abstract  = "How quickly does a fiat money become valueless? I study the
               speculative hyperinflation equilibria of continuous-time
               economies with decentralized markets where money is essential. I
               establish necessary and sufficient conditions under which money
               dies in finite time. A necessary condition is that the liquidity
               return of money grows unbounded as the value of money approaches
