  journal   = "American economic review. Insights",
  publisher = "American Economic Association",
  volume    =  3,
  number    =  4,
  pages     = "523--539",
  abstract  = "We investigate the effect of teenage driving on mortality and
               risky behaviors in the United States using a regression
               discontinuity design. We estimate that total mortality rises by
               5.84 deaths per 100,000 (15 percent) at the minimum legal driving
               age cutoff, driven by an increase in motor vehicle fatalities of
