  author    = "Rexer, Jonah M",
  journal   = "American Economic Review",
  publisher = "American Economic Association",
  volume    =  115,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "1019--1057",
  abstract  = "Multinationals in the extractive sectors of weak states face
               resource theft by armed groups. Criminality is often abetted by
               state corruption, even though firms are willing to pay for
               protection. I study indigenization in Nigeria’s oil sector, which
               increased local firms’ participation substantially. Despite lower
               quality, local firms increase output by reducing oil theft. A
