  volume    =  113,
  number    =  12,
  pages     = "3129--3172",
  abstract  = "How does the expectation that a child will receive government
               benefits in adulthood affect parental investments in the child’s
               human capital? Most parents whose children receive Supplemental
               Security Income (SSI) benefits overestimate the likelihood that
               their child will receive SSI benefits in adulthood. We present
