  pages     = "1144--1157",
  abstract  = "We study the brutal 1991–2002 Sierra Leone civil war using
               nationally representative household data on conflict experiences,
               postwar economic outcomes, local politics and collective action.
               Individuals whose households directly experienced more intense
               war violence are robustly more likely to attend community
