  pages     = "333--352",
  abstract  = "Penalty systems can very often be looked upon as corrective
               measures established in order to eliminate or reduce costly
               externalities generated by optimizing economic agents. Hence,
               penalties can be viewed as regulatory measures and their
               efficient structure should be of interest to economists. We
