  volume    =  21,
  number    =  2,
  pages     = "323--351",
  abstract  = "This article uses seven waves of panel data to test for social
               norms in labor market status. The unemployed's well‐being is
               shown to be strongly positively correlated with reference group
               unemployment (at the regional, partner, or household level). This
               result, far stronger for men, is robust to controls for
               unobserved individual heterogeneity. Panel data also show that
