  number    =  3,
  pages     = "451--472",
  abstract  = "In the past several decades, professional views on the relation
               between inflation and unemployment have gone through two stages
               and are now entering a third. The first was the acceptance of a
               stable trade-off (a stable Phillips curve). The second was the
               introduction of inflation expectations, as a variable shifting
               the short-run Phillips curve, and of the natural rate of
               unemployment, as determining the location of a vertical long-run
