  volume    =  93,
  number    =  1,
  pages     = "210--224",
  abstract  = "Liquidity constraints represent a major obstacle for potential
               migrants trying to meet the high cost of undocumented
               international migration. Some cover it by borrowing from a
               smuggling organization with a commitment to repay the loan by
               working in the destination country as bonded laborers. This paper
               compares alternative ways of financing migration and shows that
               debt bondage is optimal only if the international wage
