  number    =  1,
  pages     = "1--35",
  abstract  = "We examine the impact of enforcement on subsequent compliance
               behavior by taxpayers. Exploiting waves of randomized audits by
               the Internal Revenue Service from 2006 to 2009, we find three
               long-run responses by taxpayers. First, audits increase tax
               payments substantially in following years, but this effect is
               short-lived when third-party reporting is not available. Second,
               taxpayers with high income volatility revert to their preaudit
