  pages     = "303--321",
  abstract  = "Is it possible to trade with bandits? When government is absent,
               the superior strength of some agents makes it cheaper for them to
               violently steal what they desire from weaker agents than to use
               trade to obtain what they want. Such was the case with middlemen
               who interacted with producers in late precolonial west central
               Africa. In the face of this threat, producers employed two
               mechanisms to make exchange with middlemen possible. On the one
