  author    = "Aughinbaugh, Alison and Gittleman, Maury",
  journal   = "Journal of health economics",
  publisher = "Elsevier BV",
  volume    =  23,
  number    =  4,
  pages     = "815--838",
  abstract  = "This paper examines the impact of maternal employment during a
               child's first 3 years and during adolescence on his or her
               decisions to engage in a range of risky behaviors: smoking
               cigarettes, drinking alcohol, using marijuana and other drugs,
               engaging in sex and committing crimes. Using data from the NLSY79
               and its young adult supplement, we do not find strong evidence
