  author    = "Piette Durrance, Christine and Wang, Yang and Wolfe, Barbara",
  journal   = "Journal of health economics",
  publisher = "Elsevier BV",
  volume    =  98,
  number    =  102939,
  pages     =  102939,
  abstract  = "Abortion restrictions affect access to reproductive health care.
               Research has demonstrated that abortion restrictions (policies
               that restrict access to abortion services or cause abortion
               clinics to close) result in reductions of and delays in
               abortions. We leverage two population-based datasets to
               investigate the effects of mandatory waiting periods (MWPs), a
               restrictive state abortion policy, on the prevalence of intimate
               partner violence (IPV), one of the most common types of crime and
               a highly prevalent and costly public health problem, using data
               from the National Incident-Based Reporting System and Uniform
               Crime Report - Supplemental Homicide Reports. We hypothesize that
