               more than $60 billion per aviation disaster, whereas the
               estimated actual loss is no more than $1 billion. In two days a
               price reversal occurs. We find the effect to be greater in small
               and riskier stocks and in firms belonging to less stable
               industries. This event effect is also accompanied by an increase
