  pages     = "68--84",
  abstract  = "I analyze how informal agreements can be sustained by moral
               emotions with regard to a large class of two-player games.
               Specifically, I assume that people feel guilty if they breach an
               agreement and that the guilt increases according to the degree of
               the harm inflicted on the other. A central insight is that it is
               easier to sustain efficient informal agreements if actions are
