               model. They are also corroborated by the findings in two case
               studies in a car-manufacturing firm, briefly discussed at the end
               of the paper. It appears that the users of the information system
               who have to deal with EDP-specialists having sanctionary power
               over them (a case of power asymmetry) are less inclined to
               implement the system exactly as the user and the specialist had
