  pages     = "286--297",
  abstract  = "This paper describes a methodology for management information
               systems design which employs a formalized framework for
               significantly involving manager-users in the design process. The
               process seeks to develop a system design on the basis of a
               criterion which considers both technical cost-benefit
               considerations and the manager's perception of the potential
               utility of the system. A key element of the methodology is the
               development of descriptive and normative system models which are
               based on the concept of a “linear responsibility chart.” These
