  number    =  1,
  pages     = "69--92",
  abstract  = "It is estimated that up to 30–35 percent of the total urban
               population of the Third World (about 185 million people) live in
               squatter settlements. This paper presents, from an economic
               perspective of tenure choice under uncertainty, a unified and
               consistent theoretical framework of this phenomenon, which has
               heretofore been studied mainly by other social scientists. The
               model is able to explain why land invasions occur. Furthermore,
               it provides some insights as to why the number of squatters in an
