  volume    =  82,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "556--565",
  abstract  = "Enforcement by monitoring cannot be conditioned on the severity
               of an offense while enforcement by investigation can be. If some
               degrees of the offenses are not adequately reported or if
               investigation is too costly, the regulator must monitor and treat
               offenses of different severity quite differently. Smaller
               offenses should not be investigated; they should be deterred by
