  journal   = "Journal of criminal justice",
  publisher = "Elsevier BV",
  volume    =  86,
  number    =  102062,
  pages     =  102062,
  abstract  = "Background Predominant explanations of the victim-offender
               overlap tend to focus on shared causes, such as (low)
               self-control or risky lifestyles. Such explanations bypass the
               possibility of a causal link between victimization and offending.
               We draw on evolutionary developmental psychology and
               criminological research to propose and test the hypothesis that
               victimization induces what we refer to as a short-term mindset,
               i.e., an orientation towards the here-and-now at the expense of
