  volume    =  17,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "303--312",
  abstract  = "The ``psychometric paradigm'' developed by Slovic, Fischhoff, and
               Lichtenstein was a landmark in research about public attitudes
               toward risks. One problem with work, however, was that (at least
               initially) it did not attempt to distinguish between individuals
               or groups of people, except ``experts'' vs. ``lay people.'' This
