               police forces remain uncertain how to robustly assess organised
               crime within their own borders. To address this and contribute to
               the development of a local ‘narrative’ of organised crime we
               studied two UK neighbourhoods where organised crime was known to
               be impacting. Our study brings together data from multiple
               sources that each offer a distinct perspective: the measurable
               impact of organised crime as represented in recorded crime, the
               groups, offenders and activities recorded by the police for the
