  volume    =  26,
  number    =  1,
  pages     = "83--106",
  abstract  = "Individual demographic characteristics and aggregate population
               processes are central to many theoretical perspectives and
               empirical models of criminal behavior. Recent research
               underscores the importance of criminal and deviant behavior for
               understanding the demography of the life course and macrolevel
               population processes. We review research that explores the
