               resulting impact on judicial procedure fairness, which
               encompasses procedural participation, equality, transparency,
               rationality, timeliness, and finality. This study explores
               procedural fairness issues in China’s criminal justice system by
               focusing on applying technical investigative measures in
               drug-related cases. We have gathered a sample of 800 verdicts of
               drug-related criminal cases with 1134 defendants from China
               Judgments Online. Employing logistic regression analysis, we
               investigated the influence of extra-legal and legal factors on
