               motivations among academy recruits in the New York City Police
               Department (NYPD). Using the same survey and analysis, this study
               re-examined motivations among officers from the same NYPD recruit
               class after six years on the job, and explored both motivation
               stability and the relationships among motivations and job
               satisfaction. Results suggested that motivations have remained
