  pages     = "101--115",
  abstract  = "The experience of racism is variegated and the methods used in
               collecting data in this area are widely acknowledged to be
               flawed. This article reflects on the experience of interviewing
               older people from minority ethnic backgrounds about their quality
               of life, with specific reference to how individuals report their
               experience of racism, the reasons for reporting, and the
               circumstances surrounding the reporting of such experience. It
               demonstrates that data on the experience of racism are very much
               a consequence of the process of research. A more reflexive
               approach to research is recommended. The type of questions posed,
