  volume    =  94,
  number    =  102265,
  pages     =  102265,
  abstract  = "Purpose For the last five decades, gangs have been a criminal
               justice priority, commanding the attention of police, courts, and
               corrections. Legislative bodies and local, state, and federal
               agencies have adapted or engineered policies and practices to
               combat the influence of gangs. While these efforts have been
               subject to inquiry by researchers and media, they have largely
               been uninformed by public opinion. Methods We surveyed 1000
               adults in the United States to understand public support for five
               common yet controversial responses to gangs spearheaded by the
