               violations but not violence reduction; support for RICO fell when
               learning of the organizational structure of street gangs and the
               potential for guilt-by-association; and sentencing enhancements
               were no longer supported upon learning the financial cost.
               Conclusions Public opinion maintains a significant role in
               criminal justice policy and practice on gangs that criminologists
               should subject to research and evaluation. This research
