  volume    =  123,
  pages     = "29--39",
  abstract  = "•We sought to influence (or nudge) security behaviour in an
               experiment in 5 EU countries, n = 2024.•Coping messages were more
               effective than threat appeals in promoting secure online
               behaviour.•Risk attitudes, age and country had a significant
               effect on security behaviour. We conducted an online experiment
               (n = 2024) on a representative sample of internet users in
               Germany, Sweden, Poland, Spain and the UK to explore the effect
               of notifications on security behaviour. Inspired by protection
               motivation theory (PMT), a coping message advised participants on
