               adolescents in the Chinese setting from a lifestyle/routine
               activity perspective using a multilevel approach. These data are
               collected from a sample of 3,628 high school students in a
               southern city of China. The results of a hierarchical logistic
               regression model reveal that school contextual variables
               including school type, level of bonding to school, and school
               history are significant predictors of violent victimization while
