               economics of deterrence. Modern criminology is now poised for
               reinventing justice around the emotions of victims, offenders,
               and society. One prime example is restorative justice. Others
               include wider use of biomedical mental health treatments for
               offenders, programs to make justice officials more aware of the
               emotional impact of their words on citizens, and programs to help
               justice officials manage their own emotions. Research can advance
               theory and innovations as a basis for a new paradigm of
               “emotionally intelligent justice.”",
