               gain emotional trust and persuade victims to invest in a
               fictitious website controlled by the scammer group. The
               substantial economic loss forced the Chinese government to launch
               a series of judicial campaigns against this crime. Regardless,
               Sha Zhu Pan has not been significantly curbed but intensified and
               spread from mainland China to Southeast Asia, North America, and
               other regions. When procuring answers to this conundrum, no
               empirical studies have attempted to explore judicial aspects
               among Sha Zhu Pan cases in China. The purpose of this paper is to
               utilize focal concern theory, a conceptual framework generally
