               about the system’s regionalized vulnerability. This paper
               presents a new methodology for structural industrial
               vulnerability assessment based on production factors that enables
               to assess the regional industrial disaster vulnerability. In
               order to capture industry-specific vulnerability factors and to
               account for the processes underlying regional industrial
               vulnerability, a two-stage approach is developed. This approach
               combines a composite indicator model to assess sector-specific
               vulnerability indices (Vs) with a new regionalization method. The
