               In particular, the concurrent rise in fake news and online scams
               has shown signs of convergence in the form of fake news-scams,
               where false information is manipulated and employed in scams.
               However, literature examining this emerging phenomenon is scarce.
               As such, this study aims to deepen our understanding of this
               novel issue by exploring how scammers employ fake news in terms
               of type, channels of transmission, and persuasion techniques.
               Drawing from local case studies ( n = 90) collected from 2016 to
