               States. Specific areas examined included: presence and scope;
               administrative entity for certifying; screening and risk
               assessment protocols; minimum length of treatment; theoretical or
               conceptual orientation; treatment content; preferred or allowable
               modalities of treatment; whether research findings are mentioned;
               methods for revising standards; and minimum education and
               training required for providers. We examined trends using several
