  author    = "Levy, Jeremy M and Irvin-Erickson, Yasemin and La Vigne, Nancy",
  journal   = "Security journal",
  publisher = "Springer Nature",
  volume    =  31,
  number    =  1,
  pages     = "226--246",
  abstract  = "This article employs Routine Activities and Crime Pattern
               theories to explore the factors that lead to increased risk of
               bike theft, focusing on Washington Metropolitan Transit Authority
               Metrorail (Metro) property. Utilizing the Metro bike census and
               other data, we use negative binomial regression analysis to model
               the relationship between bike thefts and various station- and
