  volume    =  26,
  number    =  4,
  pages     = "349--366",
  abstract  = "Community-oriented policing has shaped law enforcement over the
               past 30 years, providing innovative strategies to identify and
               combat crime problems through collaborative community
               partnerships. The success of community policing strategies in
               some contexts has led some scholars and police administrators to
               call for the adoption of these programs in virtual environments
