  volume    =  13,
  number    =  9,
  pages     = "e0204454",
  abstract  = "The independent mobility (IM), defined as the freedom of young
               people to travel without adult supervision, has been related to
               the physical activity time, the acquisition of personal autonomy,
               to less intense fear of crime, and to a stronger feeling of being
               part of their community and other health and social benefits. The
