               household size as the nighttime indicator of small-areas, and
               daytime population density as their daytime indicator. The
               potential for the estimation of daytime populations across
               metropolitan regions where daytime population data are
               unavailable, is underscored by the clear tendency towards inverse
               relation of these two indicators of diurnal shift.",
