  pages     = "268--291",
  abstract  = "In general research suggests partner violence has a negative
               impact on women's employment. However, there has been limited
               examination of partner stalking and consequences for employment.
               The purpose of this study was to examine partner stalking and
               employment consequences among two samples of women. One sample
               was women who had obtained a protective order against a violent
               partner and had worked in the prior year (n = 482), about one
               half of these women were stalked by their violent partner and one
               half were not. The second study examined qualitative information
               from women recently stalked (n = 62) by a violent partner.
               Results from both studies suggest that women who were stalked by
               a violent partner were significantly more susceptible to
