  volume    =  35,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "893--912",
  abstract  = "This article analyzes the international legal framework against
               cybercrime. The international legal framework provides a solution
               to the problem in three areas: reducing discrepancies between
               national laws, introducing new powers of authorities, and
               promoting international cooperation. The study argues that the
               core documents effectiveness in the field of cybercrime
               counteraction does not appear to be dependent on the legal
               applicability of the international measures. Such factors as
