               explanations in light of observed trends. In contrast with much
               of the recent literature, we argue that the locus of the crime
               drop in the 1990s is not wholly consistent with the available
               data and that while New York City experienced substantial crime
               decreases, its uniqueness has been exaggerated. We suggest that
