               youth; gender of a child was not associated with school travel
               mode. As school travel related programmes are beginning to be
               adapted to the high-school context, our results indicate that a
               current North American model that is largely designed around
               capital improvement of transport infrastructure may not be very
               successful. Rather, programmes and initiatives should emphasize
               education, and perhaps attempt to understand and reshape the
               culture of youth mobility, in order to encourage healthy and
               sustainable travel practices.",
