  volume    =  39,
  number    =  2,
  pages     = "321--348",
  abstract  = "Previous studies have explained the transition from criminal
               propensity in youth to criminal behavior in adulthood with
               hypotheses of enduring criminal propensity, unique social
               causation, and cumulative social disadvantage. In this article we
               develop an additional hypothesis derived from the life‐course
               concept of interdependence: The effects of social ties on crime
