               review of major findings from two recent nonmetropolitan studies
               using survey data from 1,125 citizens nested in 31
               nonmetropolitan residential units (RUs) located in the state of
               Michigan. Hierarchical linear modeling results provide empirical
               evidence that the differential ability of nonmetropolitan
               Michigan residents to realize mutual trust and solidarity (i.e.,
               social cohesion) is a major source of RU variation in citizens’
