  number    =  4,
  pages     = "589--598",
  abstract  = "AbstractWe draw on the focus theory of normative conduct and
               nudge theory to experimentally test the effect of descriptive
               social norms on desired behaviors that public employees may
               engage in at suboptimal levels, namely, vaccination and
               help‐seeking. Through a series of framed randomized controlled
               trials with 19,984 public healthcare professionals, we
               demonstrate that descriptive norms—doing what the majority of
               others do—trigger conformity. Specifically, employees are more
