               research to date addresses burglary and shooting incidents. Using
               the Knox method for space–time interaction, this study analyzes
               crime data in 12 “super neighborhoods” located in Houston’s
               crime-heavy southwest quadrant to explore spatial–temporal
               clustering of three types of crime, namely, residential burglary,
