  volume    =  50,
  number    =  10,
  pages     = "1059--1091",
  abstract  = "According to the “low-cost hypothesis” (LCH), attitudes explain
               behavior only if complying with personal convictions requires
               little effort. Environmental research has seized this argument to
               explain moderate participation in pro-environmental action
               against a backdrop of rising environmental awareness. However,
