               have been identified: proactive behavior (47\% of victims),
               avoidance (30\%), and passivity (23\%). The examination of the
               association between these coping strategies and victims' fear
               reveals that female victims, whose behavior is proactive, express
               higher levels of fear than male victims and than those choosing
               avoidance or passivity strategies. Overall, the study confirms
               gender differences in both the level of fear and coping
