  pages     = "543--580",
  abstract  = "This research updates and expands upon Decker’s article “Citizen
               attitudes toward the police: a review of past findings and
               suggestions for future policy” by summarizing the findings from
               more than 100 articles on perceptions of and attitudes toward the
               police. Initially, the value of research on attitudes toward the
               police is discussed. Then the research pertaining to the impact
               of individual level variables (e.g. race) and contextual level
               variables (e.g. neighborhood) on perceptions of the police is
               reviewed. Studies of juveniles’ attitudes toward the police,
               perceptions of police policies and practices, methodological
               issues and conceptual issues are also discussed. This review of
