  author    = "Carfora, V and Caso, D and Sparks, P and Conner, M",
  journal   = "Journal of environmental psychology",
  publisher = "Elsevier BV",
  volume    =  53,
  pages     = "92--99",
  abstract  = "Self-identity is considered as a useful additional predictor in
               the theory of planned behaviour (TPB). However, previous research
               generally assessed the impact of pro-environmental self-identity
               in relation to single behaviours and no studies considered its
               potential role in moderating the impact of other predictors on
               behaviour. The present research used a within-persons approach to
               examine effects across behaviours and a longitudinal design to
               assess the moderating role of self-identity in the prediction of
               intentions and behaviours, controlling for past behaviour.
               Participants (N = 240) completed Time 1 questionnaires measuring
               TPB constructs in relation to five different pro-environmental
