  abstract  = "Over the last 40 years and more, a growing number of researchers
               have explored the links between perceptions of disorder and fear
               of criminal victimization. Many of these studies have posited a
               causal link from perceptions of disorder to subsequent fear, with
               disorderly cues in the environment signalling to individuals that
               an area is in decline and unable to control deviant behaviour.
