               correlated well with H1N1 incidence data. CONCLUSIONS: This study
               illustrates the potential of using social media to conduct
               ``infodemiology'' studies for public health. 2009 H1N1-related
               tweets were primarily used to disseminate information from
               credible sources, but were also a source of opinions and
