  volume    =  68,
  number    =  101685,
  pages     =  101685,
  abstract  = "Purpose: This study analyzes the pathways leading to violent
               offending. We examine whether the lethality of a violent crime
               could be predicted based on individuals' prior history of violent
               crime and income, and whether the trajectories of lethal
               offenders are distinguishable from the pathways of non-lethal
               offenders. Methods: We use a sample of police-reported violent
               crimes committed in Finland in 2010–2011 (N = 26,303) and
               contrast the pathways to homicide with the trajectories leading
               to petty assault, assault, aggravated assault, and attempted
               homicide. Group-based trajectory modeling is applied for
