               construct a synthetic counterfactual, we test whether calls to
               police and/or emergency hotlines varied in 2020 as people stayed
               home due to COVID-19. Across this sample, we estimate there were
               approximately 1030 more calls to police and 1671 more calls to
               emergency hotlines than would have occurred absent the pandemic.
               Policy Implications: Interagency data sharing and analysis holds
               great promise for better understanding localized trends in DV in
