  volume    =  6,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "536--551",
  abstract  = "ABSTRACTThe health consequences of gentrification are
               little-understood, and researchers have called for qualitative
               studies to uncover potential causal pathways between
               gentrification and health. Resident Researchers in a
               Participatory Action Research study of community health in nine
               gentrifying neighborhoods across the Boston area hypothesized
               that financial insecurity is one pathway through which
               gentrification might harm health. We analyze qualitative data
               from semi-structured interviews with 40 financially vulnerable
               respondents to understand how the experience of living in a
