  abstract  = "Major crime drops were experienced in the United States and most
               other industrialized countries for a decade from the early to
               mid-1990s. Yet there is little agreement over explanation or
               lessons for policy. Here it is proposed that change in the
               quantity and quality of security was a key driver of the crime
               drop. From evidence relating to vehicle theft in two countries,
               it is concluded that electronic immobilizers and central locking
