               framework for understanding how policing logics are amplified,
               contested, and resonate through popular media as part of a
               hegemonic process to sustain the PIC. We suggest that the
               scaffolding for these logics is built through rhetoric that
               normalizes the routine violence of policing ( copspeak), the ways
               in which police create and control their own image ( image work),
               and the widespread tendency of popular media to portray policing
