               position of opportunity in self‐control theory and argue that it
               should play a significant role in the theory, even if Gottfredson
               and Hirschi did not originally envision this. Next, we draw on
               routine activities theory and applications of it to individual
               offending to offer a theoretical statement of how opportunity
               should be incorporated into self‐control theory. Last, using data
