  volume    =  57,
  number    = "C",
  pages     = "142--153",
  abstract  = "Social science literature suggests that neighborhood-based visual
               cues have substantive effects on individuals' littering
               behaviors. Experimental research on this topic typically alters
               the appearance of a selected public location, and then monitors
               changes in littering due to these tightly controlled esthetic
