               were analyzed for (1) all cafeteria customers and (2) a
               longitudinal cohort of 2285 hospital employees who used the
               cafeteria regularly. INTERVENTION: After a 3-month baseline
               period, cafeteria items were labeled green (healthy); yellow
               (less healthy); or red (unhealthy) and rearranged to make healthy
               items more accessible. MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES: Proportion of
               cafeteria sales that were green or red during each 3-month period
