  number    =  2,
  pages     = "391--416",
  abstract  = "While the literature has extensively documented popular
               discontent with various types of police misconduct, little is
               known about popular support for corrective measures. Such
               information, however, would be valuable for public policy and has
               the potential to enhance public confidence in the police. This
               article, using data from a recent national survey, reports public
               attitudes toward several specific reforms in policing. Findings
               indicate, first, that race is a predictor. Blacks and Hispanics
