               in their ability to walk to or from school without an adult (OR =
               2.03), school encouragement (OR = 2.43), scheduling commitments
               (OR = 0.41), and parent-perceived convenience of driving (OR =
               0.24) were significantly associated (p < .05) with walking.
               Irrespective of gender and proximity to school, child-perceived
               convenience of walking (boys OR = 2.17 and girls OR = 1.84) and
