               highlights cybercrimes’ legal importance globally and cybercrime
               regulations during the Covid-19 times, specifically in the
               Indonesian context. Using a normative juridical approach, this
               study collected secondary data from various books, journals,
               regulatory guidelines, institutional reports, research, and the
               Internet. Additionally, a systematic literature search
               methodology was used to collect relevant secondary data from the
               most popular database, i.e., Scopus. Results revealed that
               although many nations are actively working to control
