               criminology",
  author    = "Blomberg, Thomas G and Copp, Jennifer E and Turanovic, Jillian J",
  journal   = "Annual review of criminology",
  publisher = "Annual Reviews",
  volume    =  7,
  number    =  1,
  pages     = "143--162",
  abstract  = "The relevance of criminology to matters of public policy has been
               hotly debated throughout the history of the discipline. Yet time
               and again, we have borne witness to the consequences of harmful
               criminal justice practices that do little to reduce crime or
               improve the lives of our most vulnerable populations. Given the
               urgent need for evidence-informed responses to the problems that
               face our society, we argue here that criminologists can and
               should have a voice in the process. Accordingly, this review
               describes challenges and prospects for evidence-informed
