              nonsignificant after considering adverse social conditions in
              urban neighborhoods such as low social cohesion and high
              neighborhood disorder (OR = 1.35, 95\% CI = 0.94-1.92, P = .102).
              The combined association of adverse neighborhood social conditions
              and personal crime victimization with adolescent psychotic
