  number    =  2,
  pages     = "198--212",
  abstract  = "The boom of regulatory agencies is a common global phenomenon,
               and its basics are deeply rooted in national settings, leading to
               the setting up of specific regulators. Theoretically, auditors
               must demonstrate their professional prowess, skepticism, and
               analytical procedure, and effectively communicate audit outcomes
               to the stakeholders. Interestingly, the Indian audit profession
