  volume    =  7,
  number    =  6,
  pages     = "546--570",
  abstract  = "Desistance studies have routinely focused on issues such as
               family links, employment prospects and moving away from criminal
               friends, but they have said less about the meso- and macro-level
               structural issues that might facilitate or impede the transition
               of ex-offenders to the status of more mainstream members of civil
               society.Yet, in view of the necessary interaction between agency
               and structure in producing processes of desistance, a
