               vehicles, and more stolen vehicle recoveries. Unexpectedly, the
               authors found that manual plate checking by a special auto theft
               unit (but not LPR scanning by the same unit) was associated with
               less auto theft 2 weeks after the intervention (based on both
               police crime reports and calls for police service) than the
               control group (regular nonspecialized patrol without LPR).
