               of 1,800 Istanbulians, the potential contributions of perceived
               neighborhood characteristics also are considered. Results show
               that both instrumental and normative models of regulation are
               applicable to the highly centralized and state-serving Turkish
               policing context. While the instrumental model exerts relatively
