  volume    =  47,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "373--389",
  abstract  = "While crime prevention is taken to exemplify governance in the
               'risk society', it may represent a retarded example of risk-based
               urban security. Crime prevention was unaffected by risk-based
               prevention characteristic of much 19th century government of this
               domain. The development of risk-based fire prevention, by
               contrast, was substantially in place at the turn of the 20th
               century, promoted by the convergence of insurance and other
               interests in securing property. Rather than seeing crime
