               behaviour does not always occur when needed, and the absence of
               helping during crisis is less well studied. By broadly defining a
               crisis as an extremely difficult, disruptive and dangerous
               situation, which may result in possible harm to individuals,
               groups and societies, this article reviews research focused on
               the following general question: What factors (psychological,
