  abstract  = "Abstract Cigarette littering in public spaces is an environmental
               and aesthetic problem. Broken windows theory posits that visible
               signs of anti-social behavior such as littering create the
               perception of a social norm in built environments. Cigarette
               butts on the ground then encourage people to drop theirs as well.
               We test this theory on benches of a university campus in a field
               experiment with two treatments: (1) a clean environment with no
               cigarette butts on the ground and (2) a dirty environment with 25
               cigarette butts on the ground. Our outcome variable is the number
