               landscape. For practitioners and policy makers alike, erecting
               steel gates at entrances to alleys is seen as a major initiative
               for reducing domestic burglary. In particular, in the current
               climate of economic austerity, such apparently cost-effective
               measures may seem more attractive to policy makers and planners
               alike as they struggle to maintain public confidence in the
