  volume    =  18,
  number    =  5,
  pages     = "471--483",
  abstract  = "Between 1980 and 2010 there were 1 million homicides in Brazil.
               Dramatic increases in homicide rates followed rises in
               inequality, more young men in the population, greater
               availability of firearms, and increased drug use. Nevertheless,
               disarmament legislation may have helped reduce homicide rates in
