               Developers are creating gated communities to reverse this trend,
               but their success remains unknown. This research empirically
               addresses the issues of sense of community, crime, and fear of
               crime in a comparative study of two gated and two nongated
               communities with similar attributes. Mail surveys were conducted
               in both a gated and a nongated community in two contexts: public
               housing and high-income suburban communities. Results showed that
               high-income gated community residents reported a significantly
