  volume    =  62,
  pages     = "19--29",
  abstract  = "A cooperative routing strategy for daily operations is necessary
               to maintain the effects of hotspot policing and to reduce crime
               and disorder. Existing robot patrol routing strategies are not
               suitable, as they omit the peculiarities and challenges of daily
               police patrol including minimising the average time lag between
               two consecutive visits to hotspots, as well as coordinating
