  abstract  = "In a series of recent influential papers, Anthony Bottoms and
               Justice Tankebe make the case for a ‘dialogic model’ of police
               legitimacy, wherein legitimacy is envisaged as emergent in a
               process through which the police, as power-holders, make claims
               to authority which are, in turn, responded to by audiences. Our
