  number    =  3,
  pages     = "37--60",
  abstract  = "This article discusses two schools of criminology which have been
               identified in the history of criminology, the classical school
               and the positive school. The classical school was a reaction to
               the harsh and arbitrary use of capital punishment during the
               Middle Ages. The eighteenth-century liberals advocated strict and
               precise legal definitions of crimes and punishment, set penalties
