  volume    =  51,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "197--208",
  abstract  = "Given the rapid growth of research–practice partnerships (RPPs),
               we need a framework that helps the field understand how RPPs can
               facilitate organizational learning in service of local
               educational improvement and transformation. Drawing on
               sociocultural and organizational learning theories, we argue that
               learning can happen for the organizations engaged in RPPs at the
               boundaries of research and practice. Such learning is evident
