               proposed 750 MW offshore wind farm in North Wales, using group
               discussions and questionnaires distributed to local residents in
               two coastal towns (n = 488). Results indicate significant
               differences between each town's residents in their responses to
               the project, and how opposition arises from nature/industry
               symbolic contradictions: between a place represented in terms of
               scenic beauty that provides a restorative environment for
               residents and visitors, and a wind farm that will industrialise
               the area and ‘fence’ in the bay. In one of the towns, the data
               suggests that contradiction between project and place was
               experienced as a threat to identity for those with strong place
