  pages     = "73--83",
  abstract  = "Law enforcement is a career that offers long-term employment;
               however, not everyone who enters the profession stays until they
               retire. Because the costs of employing a police officer can be
               significant to both the organization and the individual seeking
               to pursue and maintain a career in law enforcement, identifying
               ways to reduce police turnover is important. This study captures
               the experiences of officers who left prematurely, whether
               voluntarily or involuntarily, to help identify what agencies can
               do to keep officers long term. Data for this exploratory study
