  pages     = "775--808",
  abstract  = "With a focus on the implementation of women’s police stations
               (WPS), we posit that local policies that address violence against
               women can result in positive feedback effects on institutional
               legitimacy. We theorize that WPS increase police legitimacy among
               women by improving perceptions of personal safety and government
               responsiveness. To test our hypotheses, we rely on municipal and
               public opinion data from more than 100 municipalities in Brazil.
               The results of our multilevel analysis indicate that WPS produce
               positive feedback effects among women, resulting in higher trust
