               higher fear of crime than men. One explanation for these
               differences is perceptually contemporaneous offenses (Warr 1984)
               that link fear of one crime, like sexual assault, to a variety of
               perceptually related crimes. When fear of rape is included in
               fear models the sex-gap is generally reduced. Recent work in the
