  volume    =  8,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "147--176",
  abstract  = "News coverage of intimate partner homicide can reveal and
               reproduce societal assumptions and beliefs that may influence
               social and political responses to violence against women. This
               study analyzes all male-perpetrated intimate partner homicides
               reported in three daily newspapers in Toronto, Canada within two
               separate time periods (1975-1979 and 1998-2002) to explore if and
