              on the OAFEM consistent with higher risk for financial
              exploitation. Self-reported physical and mental health, male
              gender, and younger age were also related to increased risk.
              CONCLUSIONS: Results indicated that numeracy is a significant risk
              factor for elder financial exploitation after controlling for
              other commonly reported variables. These findings are consistent
              with the broader literature relating numeracy to wealth and debt
