  volume    =  33,
  number    =  4,
  pages     = "543--571",
  abstract  = "S. Kaplan suggested that one outcome of mental fatigue may be an
               increased propensity for outbursts of anger and even violence. If
               so, contact with nature, which appears to mitigate mental
               fatigue, may reduce aggression and violence. This study
               investigated that possibility in a setting and population with
               relatively high rates of aggression: inner-city urban public
               housing residents. Levels of aggression were compared for 145
               urban public housing residents randomly assigned to buildings
