               legitimacy of the police. Most of this research focused on police
               agencies in the United States, and little research had been
               conducted on citizen perceptions of the police in Asian
               countries. This study sought to fill this void through an
               analysis of citizen perceptions of the police in South Korea. To
               address these issues, telephone interview survey data gathered
               from 11,500 randomly selected citizens were obtained in the
               rapidly industrializing country, South Korea. Several sets of
