  abstract  = "Objectives:To examine whether victim, offender, and relationship
               characteristics increase the risk and frequency of intimate
               partner violence (IPV). The effect of separation length on the
               risk of IPV is also evaluated.Methods:Using abuse incident data (
               N = 4,960) from IPV victims ( n = 497), who accessed a
               health-care facility over a one-year period, between-individual
               differences in the frequency and timing of abuse were assessed.
