               2020. These referred to 16 studies involving 4021 participants.
               Findings The findings, except for one study, revealed consistent
               evidence of bias towards victims of sexual revictimization, which
               related to higher levels of disbelief and victim-blame, and other
               factors. Complainants were blamed most by women when the context
               was perceived as risky. Conclusions There were several
