               crime incident data. Methods The Indianapolis Metropolitan Police
               Department provided 2016 crime incident data for five crime
               types: (1) shootings, (2) robberies, (3) residential burglaries,
               (4) theft of automobiles, and (5) theft from automobiles. The
               incident data were geocoded using a dual ranges algorithm and a
               composite algorithm. First, descriptive analysis of the distances
               between the two point patterns were conducted. Second, repeat and
