  volume    =  32,
  number    =  2,
  pages     = "283--304",
  abstract  = "Objectives: This study explores preference variation in location
               choice strategies of residential burglars. Applying a model of
               offender target selection that is grounded in assertions of the
               routine activity approach, rational choice perspective, crime
               pattern and social disorganization theories, it seeks to address
               the as yet untested assumption that crime location choice
