               the social and physical environment rather than mass media
               sensationalism may ultimately account for the fear experienced by
               some urban communities. The discussion is based on a content
               analysis of the local daily evening newspaper1 (which is further
               discussed in Smith, forthcoming), and on the results of a
               household survey conducted in north central Birmingham. The
               survey design, implementation and results are reported in more
               detail in Smith (1982a, 1983). Representatives of 531 randomly
               sampled households were interviewed from a target sample of 690
               (62 vacant dwellings, 22 non-contacts and 75 refusals comprise
