  volume    =  37,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "513--548",
  abstract  = "This study explores two issues about police legitimacy. The first
               issue is the relative importance of police legitimacy in shaping
               public support of the police and policing activities, compared to
               the importance of instrumental judgments about (1) the risk that
               people will be caught and sanctioned for wrongdoing, (2) the
