               autocorrelation patterns has increased post-COVID-19 Pandemic for
               total reported frauds, percentage of frauds reporting a loss and
               total losses, and it has reduced for the median loss.Practical
               implicationsThe sustained spatial autocorrelation in total losses
               underscores an elevated interconnectedness in economic and social
               dynamics among neighboring states. This implies that states in
