  pages     = "359--371",
  abstract  = "The popular incivilities hypothesis suggests physical
               incivilities, such as unkempt lawns and litter, and weak social
               ties with neighbors encourage crime. Despite a strong impact on
               policing policies and public awareness, this hypothesis has
               seldom been tested. We extend this basic model to test whether
