  volume    =  26,
  number    =  2,
  pages     = "183--210",
  abstract  = "Youths' exposure to school violence is ecologically patterned,
               occurring disproportionately in public schools located in urban
               disadvantaged communities. We know less, however, about how
               situational processes and environmental contexts shape school
               violence. In addition, limited research has examined the
               reciprocal nature of school and neighborhood conflicts. Here we
