  volume    =  64,
  number    =  12,
  pages     = "1636--1659",
  abstract  = "Recent experiments show that offender decision making is
               characterized by the use of cognitive heuristics. Questions
               remain about what this means for deterrence research and policy.
               I argue that the primary task is to identify ways to leverage
               decision-making biases to reduce crime. I outline three avenues
