  abstract  = "One perspective on homicide clearance by arrest argues that
               clearance is influenced by police discretion based on victim
               characteristics. Another suggests that immediate situational
               characteristics, related to physical evidence and information,
               are more important in clearing homicides. Using event history
               analysis, this study examined the effects of victim and
               situational characteristics on homicide clearance for 1579 murder
               incidents from the 2002 National Incident-Based Reporting System
               (NIBRS). Unlike the logistic regression approach typically used
               in murder clearance research, event history analysis considers
               the length of time to clearance, increasing the accuracy of
               estimates. The current analysis found that incidents with female
