  volume    =  88,
  number    =  2,
  pages     = "95--105",
  abstract  = "At a time when police agencies across the western world are
               struggling to maintain an effective service and also support and
               retain legitimacy within communities, important questions have
               been asked as to how this is to be achieved. The changes imposed
               upon police agencies in the UK, for example, mean that there
               could be a reduction in the number of front-line uniform officers
               and a lack of ‘engagement’ with ordinary members of the community
               which ultimately may have an impact upon the legitimacy of the
