  volume    =  59,
  number    =  7,
  pages     = "1006--1035",
  abstract  = "Prior research indicates that individual perceptions of the risk
               of punishment for criminal behavior are unrelated to actual risks
               of punishment in the areas in which individuals reside. It could
               be argued, however, that the relevant policy question is whether
               variation in actual punishment levels affects average perceptions
               of risk among aggregates. Scholars have argued that there is
               “collective wisdom” in the perceptions of collectivities of
