  volume    =  15,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "229--240",
  abstract  = "AbstractIn recent years there has been a rapid growth in
               quasi‐policing organizations throughout England and Wales. Public
               awareness and understanding of their roles and functions within
               the community has not been explored. While the community's desire
               for a uniformed presence on the streets remains strong, practical
               implementation through traditional public policing appears to
               grow more difficult. In order to satisfy this demand, the
               government has developed the concept of a ‘policing family’ made
               up of both traditional and new policing agencies. These agencies
               are public, private, and hybrid in nature and organization. There
