               posed by the Millennium bug in 1999 in the Netherlands. The study
               systematically examined the risk perception of both general
               public and computer experts with respect to the Millennium bug,
               assessing a potential discrepancy between the layman's and the
               expert's judgement, as has been observed in other risk areas. Two
               surveys were fielded, the first aimed at a random sample of the
