              increased F\&V purchasing. We also observe a significant
              interaction between cognitive load and price discounting. We find
              discounted bundles are more effective in the absence of cognitive
              load, but non-discounted bundles are more effective when shoppers
              are under cognitive load. Although more research is warranted, our
              findings suggest that when shopping under cognitive load, it is
              possible that discounts impose additional cognitive strain on the
