  number    =  3,
  pages     = "27--37",
  abstract  = "Although most commentators have dated their arrival to the 1980s,
               the use of public CCTV systems by the British police has a
               history that stretches back 40 years. Initial experiments in the
               1960s with CCTV in London and Liverpool were unsuccessful due to
               the high cost of cabling. The first permanent use was the
               surveillance of political demonstrations in central London. This
               fitted into existing police operational requirements and
               structures, and continued a process of centralization and
