  volume    =  53,
  number    =  1,
  pages     =  94,
  abstract  = "Using Donald Black's theory of self-help, and drawing on the
               collective security model and the ``fear and loathing''
               hypothesis, this paper examines factors influencing defensive
               weapon ownership. Interview data from 9,021 randomly selected
               households in 59 residential neighborhoods are used to assess the
               association between household and neighborhood characteristics
               and decisions to purchase weapons for self-protection. Findings
