  number    =  8,
  pages     = "766--775",
  abstract  = "Social norms are sustained and disseminated, both implicitly and
               explicitly, through the act of communication. As a result,
               communication researchers have sought to classify and target
               normative perceptions to enact social change. In line with this
               research, the current study investigated whether perceptions of
               past normative behavior, referred to here as historical norms,
               were significantly related to current behavior. Using the theory
               of normative behavior as a guiding framework, two studies were
               conducted to assess whether college student drinking behavior was
               related to one of two perceived historical drinking norms
