  volume    =  14,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "299--320",
  abstract  = "‘Fear of crime’ has aroused considerable academic debate, with
               criticisms both of exactly what is being measured and analysis of
               the relationship between fear and risk. At the same time,
               national and international surveys have increased reliance on a
               select ‘package’ of measures of fear. Using more precise
               questions from a rural crime survey conducted as part of the 2001
