  publisher = "Informa UK Limited",
  volume    =  24,
  number    =  4,
  pages     = "399--425",
  abstract  = "In this research we explore the interaction between gender and
               perceived risk of victimization on levels of fear of crime. Much
               of the previous research on the effects of gender on fear of
               crime assumes that crimes are not gendered and that the effects
               of gender would operate the same regardless of type of crime.
               Challenging this assumption, we examine crimes that
               disproportionately victimize women or men. We find that there is
               greater nuance in both fear of crime and perception of risk when
               explored in this way. In fact, men's fear of crime actually
               surpasses women's fear at high levels of perceived risk for those
               crimes in which men are more likely to be victimized. We offer
