  volume    =  89,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "1449--1469",
  abstract  = "What should researchers do when their baseline model is
               falsified? We recommend reporting the set of parameters that are
               consistent with minimally nonfalsified models. We call this
               thefalsification adaptive set(FAS). This set generalizes the
               standard baseline estimand to account for possible falsification.
               Importantly, it does not require the researcher to select or
               calibrate sensitivity parameters. In the classical linear IV
               model with multiple instruments, we show that the FAS has a
               simple closed‐form expression that only depends on a few 2SLS
               coefficients. We apply our results to an empirical study of roads
               and trade. We show how the FAS complements traditional
               overidentification tests by summarizing the variation in
               estimates obtained from alternative nonfalsified models.",
