  volume    =  36,
  number    = "3-4",
  pages     = "1745--1771",
  abstract  = "Intimate partner violence (IPV) is a pervasive social problem
               requiring multiple levels of intervention across sectors. Women
               experiencing IPV often seek assistance from police. Such
               help-seeking efforts are frequently perceived as problematic by
               both victims and police. A deeper understanding of victims' needs
