               respect to demonstrating that multiple victimisation is robust
               across crime types and method of study. Nine different research
               methods suggest a similar pattern of the distribution of
               victimisation; a small proportion of the population experience a
               large proportion of all crime. In the British Crime Survey, 70\%
               of all incidents were reported by the 14\% of respondents who are
               multiple victims (a conservative figure). With respect to
               significance, victimisation should not be studied without fully
               accounting for multiple victimisation. Many areas of policy and
