  pages     = "115--133",
  abstract  = "A program is economically efficient if its monetary benefits
               outweigh its monetary costs. Discussions of the economic
               efficiency of correctional intervention and other crime and
               offender prevention programs can be very persuasive and have
               gained wide appeal in political, policy, and academic settings.
