  author    = "Hope, Andrew",
  journal   = "British educational research journal",
  publisher = "Wiley",
  volume    =  35,
  number    =  6,
  pages     = "891--907",
  abstract  = "Burgeoning fears for safety in UK schools have resulted in a
               rapid growth in the use of various security measures, most
               notably closed‐circuit television (CCTV) systems. Utilising
               semi‐structured interviews and non‐participant observation this
               research examines how CCTV is used in schools, explores the
               manner in which this facilitates social control and considers the
               wider implications of such surveillance technology. It is argued
