  number    =  1,
  pages     = "155--186",
  abstract  = "OBJECTIVES: The widespread use of camera surveillance in public
               places offers criminologists the opportunity to systematically
               and unobtrusively observe crime, their main subject matter. The
               purpose of this essay is to inform the reader of current
               developments in research on crimes caught on camera. METHODS: We
               address the importance of direct observation of behavior and
               review criminological studies that used observational methods,
               with and without cameras, including the ones published in this
