  address   = "Kidlington",
  volume    =  79,
  pages     = "45--52",
  abstract  = "The importance of understanding crime in the United States
               assumed enhanced protrusion in the wake of the increased crime
               rates year by year in certain cities. Neighborhood social
               demographic variables have been largely used to measure their
               associations with crime. Other than those social factors, street
               lighting is a feature of urban and suburban settlement which is
