               Previous research has drawn mixed conclusions about the
               relationship between street lighting and crime, and the effect of
               streetlights on neighborhood crime is not entirely definitive. To
               address this challenge, we examined the spatial associations
               between street light density, neighborhood social disorganization
               characteristics and crime (e.g., burglary, vehicle theft, weapons
               offenses, etc.) in Detroit, Michigan in 2014. Using the street
