  volume    =  27,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "431--446",
  abstract  = "In England and Wales, concern over policing often reflects a
               perception of a halcyon period, epitomised by community policing,
               when the police operated on a local level and were well known to
               the communities they policed. To some extent, images of rural
               policing are a modern‐day representation of this idyll, and
