               relying too heavily on volunteers. Despite the establishment of a
               Council for Offender Rehabilitation Reform in 2006 and consequent
               legislative clarification of the roles of professional probation
               officers (PPOs) and volunteer probation officers (VPOs), the
               repeat offender rate has been increasing and the prevention of
               recidivism remains an urgent issue in criminal justice in Japan.
