               elected officials, specifically chief prosecutors, to address
               disparate treatment through criminal justice reforms. Elected
               prosecutors within across several jurisdictions have attempted to
               address these concerns by adopting “smart-on-crime” policies.
               However, the extent to which chief prosecutors have adopted such
               policies has been unexplored empirically. Additionally, little is
               known about prosecutors’ support for these changes in smaller
