  volume    =  20,
  number    =  2,
  pages     = "186--207",
  abstract  = "In this article, we argue that past efforts to distinguish among
               types of intimate partner violence in general survey data have
               committed a critical error--using data on current spouses to
               develop operationalizations of intimate terrorism and situational
               couple violence. We use ex-spouse data from the National Violence
               Against Women Survey (NVAWS) to develop new operationalizations.
