  journal   = "BMC public health",
  publisher = "Springer Science and Business Media LLC",
  volume    =  20,
  number    =  1,
  pages     =  1650,
  abstract  = "BACKGROUND: Strong evidence demonstrates that social support
               plays a key role in facilitating preventive health behaviors. The
               aim of the current study was to assess the effects of perceived
               social support on compliance with stay-at-home orders in response
               to a COVID-19 outbreak during the Persian New Year (Nowruz)
