               comparison is conducted by analyzing the data of General Social
               Surveys (GSS) and Japanese General Social Surveys (JGSS) held in
               2000.The findings reveal that in the United States, women, old
               people, and low-income groups are more likely to perceive the
               risk of crime; this perception can be attributed to their
