  volume    =  7,
  number    =  1,
  pages     = "1--29",
  abstract  = "We compare homicide rates in two quite similar cities with vastly
               different execution risks. Singapore had an execution rate close
               to one per million per year until an explosive 20‐fold increase
               in 1994–1995 and 1996 to a level that we show was probably the
               highest in the world. Then, over the next 11 years, Singapore
