               homicides?",
  author    = "Hjalmarsson, R",
  journal   = "American law and economics review",
  publisher = "Oxford University Press (OUP)",
  volume    =  11,
  number    =  2,
  pages     = "310--334",
  abstract  = "The vast majority of death penalty studies use geographically or
               temporally aggregated data. Such aggregation can make it
               virtually impossible to identify small amounts of variation in
               homicides due to executions. Therefore, this study uses data that
               are disaggregated down to daily and city levels to test whether
               executions have a short-term deterrent effect. Little consistent
               evidence is found that Texas executions deter Dallas, San
