  volume    =  94,
  number    =  1,
  pages     = "115--133",
  abstract  = "An important challenge in the crime literature is to isolate
               causal effects of police on crime. Following a terrorist attack
               on the main Jewish center in Buenos Aires, Argentina, in July
               1994, all Jewish institutions received police protection. Thus,
               this hideous event induced a geographical allocation of police
               forces that can be presumed exogenous in a crime regression.
