  volume    =  10,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "315--344",
  abstract  = "Lead pollution is consistently linked to cognitive and behavioral
               impairments, yet little is known about the benefits of public
               health interventions for children exposed to lead. This paper
               estimates the long-term impacts of early life interventions
               (e.g., lead remediation, nutritional assessment, medical
