  volume    =  15,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "150--182",
  abstract  = "Courts routinely use low cash bail as a financial incentive to
               ensure released defendants appear in court and abstain from
               crime. This can create burdens for defendants with little
               empirical evidence on its efficacy. We exploit a
               prosecutor-driven reform that led to a sharp reduction in low
