  volume    =  97,
  number    =  459,
  pages     = "872--882",
  abstract  = "This article suggests very simple three-step estimators for
               censored quantile regression models with a separation restriction
               on the censoring probability. The estimators are theoretically
               attractive (i.e., asymptotically as efficient as the celebrated
               Powell's censored least absolute deviation estimator). At the
               same time, they are conceptually simple and have trivial
               computational expenses. They are especially useful in samples of
               small size or models with many regressors, with desirable
               finite-sample properties and small bias. The separation
               restriction costs a small reduction of generality relative to the
               canonical censored regression quantile model, yet its main
               plausible features remain intact. The estimator can also be used
               to estimate a large class of traditional models, including the
               normal Amemiya–Tobin model and many accelerated failure and
               proportional hazard models. We illustrate the approach with an
               extramarital affairs example and contrast our findings with those
               of Fair.",
