  author    = "Gaviria, Alejandro",
  journal   = "Journal of development economics",
  publisher = "Elsevier BV",
  volume    =  61,
  number    =  1,
  pages     = "1--25",
  abstract  = "This paper presents an explanation of the recent escalation of
               violent crime in Colombia. The paper considers three implicit
               models that isolate different types of externalities among
               criminals. In the first model, criminals make crime more
               appealing to nearby residents by congesting the law enforcement
               system and, hence, lowering the probability of punishment. In the
               second model, the interaction of career criminals and local
               crooks speeds up the diffusion of criminal know-how and criminal
               technology. In the third model, the daily contact of youth with
               criminal adults and criminal peers results in the erosion of
