               D.E.A. (Eds.), Handbook of Applied Economic Statistics. Marcel
               Dekker, New York] and in the panel data context by Baltagi et al.
               [2003. Testing panel data regression models with spatial error
               correlation. Journal of Econometrics 117, 123–150]. The second is
               the LM tests for the error component panel data model with serial
               correlation derived by Baltagi and Li [1995. Testing AR(1)
               against MA(1) disturbances in an error component model. Journal
               of Econometrics 68, 133–151]. Hence, the joint LM test derived in
               this paper encompasses those derived in both strands of earlier
               works. In fact, in the context of our general model, the earlier
               LM tests become marginal LM tests that ignore either serial
               correlation over time or spatial error correlation. The paper
               then derives conditional LM and LR tests that do not ignore these
               correlations and contrast them with their marginal LM and LR
               counterparts. The small sample performance of these tests is
