  pages     = "2367--2420",
  abstract  = "Self-selected migration presents one potential explanation for
               why observed returns to a college education in local labor
               markets vary widely even though U.S. workers are highly mobile.
               To assess the impact of self-selection on estimated returns, this
               paper first develops a Roy model of mobility and earnings where
