               selection process. This paper develops an alternative econometric
               methodology that combines Lee's (1983) parametric maximum order
               statistic approach to reduce the dimensionality of the error
               terms with more recent work on semiparametric estimation of
               selection models (e.g., Ahn and Powell (1993)). The resulting
               semiparametric correction is easy to implement and can be adapted
               to a variety of other polychotomous choice problems. The
               empirical work, which uses 1990 U.S. Census data, confirms the
