  journal   = "Econometrica",
  publisher = "Wiley Online Library",
  abstract  = "We propose a new methodology for structural estimation of
               infinite horizon dynamic discrete choice models. We combine the
               dynamic programming (DP) solution algorithm with the Bayesian
               Markov chain Monte Carlo algorithm into a single algorithm that
               solves the DP problem and estimates the parameters
               simultaneously. As a result, the computational burden of
               estimating a dynamic model becomes comparable to that of a static
               model. Another feature of our algorithm is that even though the
               number of grid points on the state variable is small per
