  volume    =  102,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "267--272",
  abstract  = "In spite of the common wisdom that poverty breeds terrorism,
               econometric tests usually find that terrorism is influenced by
               population and various measures of democratic freedom, but not
               per capita GDP. Unlike previous studies, we use a data set
               containing separate measures of domestic and transnational
               terrorism and estimate models allowing for a nonlinear
               relationship between terrorism and poverty. When we account for
