  volume    =  63,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "885--901",
  abstract  = "Private governments, found in planned developments and
               condominiums, are increasingly common methods of delivering local
               services to residents. This paper provides the first empirical
               study of their impact on local public finance. A novel data set
               of homeowners' associations allows construction of a panel of
               private governments in California. Panel methods test whether
               public expenditures respond to private government prevalence.
