  abstract  = "This paper studies inter-jurisdictional competition in the fight
               against crime and its impact on occupational choice and the
               allocation of capital. In a world where capital is mobile,
               jurisdictions are inhabited by individuals who choose to become
               either workers or criminals. Because the return of the two
