  volume    =  96,
  number    = "5-6",
  pages     = "485--494",
  abstract  = "We estimate social externalities of tax evasion in a model where
               congestion of the auditing resources of local tax authorities
               generates a social multiplier. Identification is based on a
               contrast of the variance of tax evasion at different levels of
               aggregation. We use a unique data set that contains audits of
               about 80,000 small businesses and professionals in Italy and also
               provides an exact measure of reference groups in our model. We
