  author    = "Swensen, Isaac D",
  journal   = "Journal of public economics",
  publisher = "Elsevier BV",
  volume    =  122,
  pages     = "13--30",
  abstract  = "Drug-overdose deaths, which have more than doubled over the past
               decade, represent a growing public-health concern. Though
               substance-abuse treatment may be effective in reducing drug
               abuse, evidence for a causal effect of treatment on drug-related
               mortality is lacking. I analyze the effect of substance-abuse
               treatment on mortality by exploiting county-level variation in
               treatment facilities driven by facility openings and closings.
