               in performance between un-monitored classes in schools with an
               external examiner and un-monitored classes in schools without
               external monitoring. We find that the overall effect of having an
               external examiner in the class is to reduce the proportion of
               correct answers by 5.5 to 8.5\% – depending on the grade and the
