               of 236 US MSA the paper finds that greater agency fragmentation
               leads to less law enforcement effort (resources), but also to
               less crime! This seemingly contradictory result is robust to many
               alternative specifications. To explain the result a model is
               developed in which a unilateral increase in local law enforcement
               effort has the effect of “spatially displacing” criminals as well
