  number    =  4,
  pages     = "733--783",
  abstract  = "The recent rise in wage inequality is usually attributed to
               skill‐biased technical change (SBTC), associated with new
               computer technologies. We review the evidence for this
               hypothesis, focusing on the implications of SBTC for overall wage
               inequality and for changes in wage differentials between groups.
