  pages     = "489--522",
  abstract  = "This paper examines how job displacement and physical disability
               suffered by a spouse affects the probability that the person's
               marriage ends in divorce. According to the standard economic
               model of marriage, the arrival of new information about a
               partner's earning capacity that a negative earnings shock conveys
               might affect the gains that the couple believes it will receive
               from remaining married. Shocks may therefore affect divorce
