  number    =  4,
  pages     = "1239--1267",
  abstract  = "This paper studies whether structural properties of friendship
               networks affect individual outcomes in education. We first
               develop a model that shows that, at the Nash equilibrium, the
               outcome of each individual embedded in a network is proportional
               to her Katz-Bonacich centrality measure. This measure takes into
               account both direct and indirect friends of each individual but
