  number    =  2,
  pages     = "858--898",
  abstract  = "Abstract We explore the impact of rising incomes at the top of
               the distribution on spatial sorting patterns within large U.S.
               cities. We develop and quantify a spatial model of a city with
               heterogeneous agents and non-homothetic preferences for
               neighbourhoods with endogenous amenity quality. As the rich get
               richer, demand increases for the high-quality amenities available
