  volume    =  14,
  number    =  4,
  pages     = "680--722",
  abstract  = "How should law enforcement resources be allocated to minimize the
               harms from flexible, chain-form trafficking organizations? I show
               that optimal interventions focus on one target, the feeding
               source (decapitation) or the revenue-generating tail
               (amputation). Decapitation dismantles the crime chain under large
               budgets but induces maximal expansion otherwise, whereas
