  publisher = "American Economic Association",
  volume    =  16,
  number    =  1,
  pages     = "121--156",
  abstract  = "This paper identifies an important spillover associated with
               public health insurance: reduced incarceration. In 1990, Congress
               passed legislation that increased Medicaid eligibility for
               individuals born after September 30, 1983. We show that Black
               children born just after the cutoff are 5 percent less likely to
               be incarcerated by age 28, driven primarily by a decrease in
               incarcerations connected to financially motivated offenses.
               Children of other races, who experienced almost no gain in
