  pages     = "118--163",
  abstract  = "We estimate intergenerational income mobility in Italy using
               administrative data from tax returns. Our estimates of mobility
               are higher than prior work using survey data and indirect
               methods. The rankrank slope of parent-child income is 0.22,
               compared to 0.18 in Denmark and 0.34 in the United States. The
