  author    = "Ali, S Nageeb and Miller, David A",
  journal   = "American Economic Journal. Microeconomics",
  publisher = "American Economic Association",
  volume    =  14,
  number    =  4,
  pages     = "200--217",
  abstract  = "Many markets rely on traders truthfully communicating who has
               cheated in the past and ostracizing those traders from future
               trade. This paper investigates when truthful communication is
               incentive compatible. We find that if each side has a myopic
               incentive to deviate, then communication incentives are satisfied
               only when the volume of trade is low. By contrast, if only one
               side has a myopic incentive to deviate, then communication
               incentives do not constrain the volume of supportable trade.
