  pages     = "795--812",
  abstract  = "Because increasing a bank's capital requirement to improve the
               stability of the financial system imposes costs upon the bank, a
               regulator should ideally be able to prove beyond a reasonable
               doubt that banks classified as systemically risky really do
               create systemic risk before subjecting them to this capital
