  volume    =  101,
  pages     = "167--178",
  abstract  = "We provide a theoretical and empirical study of the relation
               between financial development and the size of the underground
               economy. In our theoretical framework agents allocate investment
               between a low-return technology which can be operated with
               internal funds, and a high-return technology which requires
               external finance. Firms can reduce the cost of funding by
               disclosing part or all of their assets and pledging them as
