  author    = "Jennings, Colin and Sanchez-Pages, Santiago",
  journal   = "Journal of development economics",
  publisher = "Elsevier BV",
  volume    =  124,
  pages     = "157--167",
  abstract  = "This paper analyzes the role of external conflict as a force that
               can create social capital. Hostile inter-group interactions can
               help to resolve intra-group social dilemmas but these potential
               gains must be weighed against the insecurity of hostile relations
               with an out-group. Our central result is that the presence of an
               outside threat can induce higher levels of social capital either
