  number    =  1,
  pages     = "129--181",
  abstract  = "Abstract We evaluate the unintended effects of Universal Credit
               (UC), a monumental welfare reform that has increased the
               stringency of the UK social security payment system. We exploit
               the rollout of UC across constituencies, targeting first-time
               claimants, predominantly young males. Using monthly data from
               2010 to 2019 for England and Wales, we first document the
               negative economic impacts of UC, showing it has led to an
