  author    = "Cardazzi, Alexander and McCannon, Bryan C and Humphreys, Brad R
               and Rodriguez, Zachary",
  journal   = "Journal of law, economics, \& organization",
  publisher = "Oxford University Press (OUP)",
  volume    =  40,
  number    =  2,
  pages     = "267--288",
  abstract  = "Abstract Domestic violence generates long-term effects on
               offenders, victims, and other household members. While coercive
               behavior explains some family violence, aggression can also be
               reactive, triggered by emotional stimulus. Insight into triggers
               of family violence can inform policy and mitigate abusive
               behavior. Card, D. and G. B. Dahl. (2011). “Family Violence and
               Football: The Effect of Unexpected Emotional Cues on Violent
               Behavior,” 126 The Quarterly Journal of Economics 103–43
               undertook a novel analysis of family violence triggers using
