  author    = "Lo Prete, Anna and Revelli, Federico",
  journal   = "Journal of law, economics, \& organization",
  publisher = "Oxford University Press (OUP)",
  volume    =  37,
  number    =  1,
  pages     = "168--197",
  abstract  = "Abstract Using data on mayoral elections in large Italian cities
               during the 2000s, we investigate whether and how voter turnout
               affects city performance across a number of dimensions. To
               address the issue of voter turnout endogeneity and identify the
               transmission mechanism, we exploit exogenous variation in
               participation rates in mayoral elections due to anticipated
               shocks (concurrence of local and national elections) and
