  abstract  = "This article revisits the long-standing issue of the determinants
               of health outcomes. We make two contributions to the literature.
               First, we use a large and comprehensive US county level health
               data set that has only recently become available. This data set
               includes five measures of health outcomes and 24 health risk
               factors in the categories of health behaviors, clinical care,
               social and economic factors, and physical environment. Second, to
               distinguish causality from correlation, we implement an emerging
               data-driven method to study the causal factors of health
               outcomes. Among all included potential health risk factors, we
