               state-level changes that have been used to study price effects,
               but the consequences have not been assessed due to the lack of a
               control group. Here we develop and implement a novel method for
               utilizing interstate heterogeneity to estimate the aggregate
               effects of a federal tax increase on rates of injury fatality and
               crime. We provide evidence that the relative importance of
