  publisher = "Elsevier BV",
  volume    =  30,
  number    =  5,
  pages     = "1032--1043",
  abstract  = "Many recent writings in health policy have proposed that health
               be valued directly and in monetary terms using the new well-being
               valuation method. Yet there is no clear consensus on what the
               best measure of individual's experience may be for the evaluation
               process. To shed light on this issue, monetary values for a
               number of health problems are compared across different
               well-being measures within the same UK data set. We find that,
