  volume    =  100,
  number    =  2,
  pages     = "326--350",
  abstract  = "Building on the pioneering study by Beck, Demirguc-Kunt, and
               Levine (2006), this study examines the effects of media ownership
               and concentration on corruption in bank lending using a unique
               World Bank data set covering more than 5,000 firms across 59
               countries. We find strong evidence that state ownership of media
