  journal   = "Journal of financial economics",
  publisher = "Elsevier BV",
  volume    =  58,
  number    = "1-2",
  pages     = "261--300",
  abstract  = "This paper evaluates the empirical relation between the level of
               financial intermediary development and (i) economic growth, (ii)
               total factor productivity growth, (iii) physical capital
               accumulation, and (iv) private savings rates. We use (a) a pure
               cross-country instrumental variable estimator to extract the
               exogenous component of financial intermediary development, and
               (b) a new panel technique that controls for biases associated
               with simultaneity and unobserved country-specific effects. After
               controlling for these potential biases, we find that (1)
               financial intermediaries exert a large, positive impact on total
               factor productivity growth, which feeds through to overall GDP
