  volume    =  73,
  number    =  4,
  pages     = "978--1016",
  abstract  = "Between 1933 and 1973 the federal government funded the
               construction of over 1 million units of low-rent housing. Using
               county-level data, I find that communities with high densities of
               public housing had lower median family income, lower median
               property values, lower population density, and a higher
