  publisher = "Cambridge University Press (CUP)",
  volume    =  83,
  number    =  4,
  pages     = "1057--1100",
  abstract  = "Napoléon Bonaparte revolutionized the practice of war with his
               reliance on a mass national army and large-scale conscription.
               This system faced one major obstacle: draft evasion. This article
               discusses Napoléon’s response to widespread draft evasion. First,
               we show that draft dodging rates across France varied with
               geographic characteristics. Second, we provide evidence that the
               regime adopted a strategy of discriminatory conscription
               enforcement by setting a lower (higher) conscription rate for
               those regions where the enforcement of conscription was more
               (less) costly. Finally, we show that this strategy resulted in a
               rapid fall in draft dodging rates across France.",
