  number    =  1,
  pages     = "271--283",
  abstract  = "In dealing with peer punishment as a cooperation enforcement
               device, laboratory studies have typically concentrated on
               discretionary sanctioning, allowing players to castigate each
               other arbitrarily. By contrast, in real life punishments are
               often meted out only insofar as punishers are entitled to punish
