               data show that the majority of advertisers and users of Backpage
               and Craigslist’s personals quickly moved to other (often
               off-shore) commercial sex advertising portals. Our results
               highlight the challenges that governments face in reducing online
               sex trafficking, as the market for commercial sex advertising
               appears agile enough to quickly disperse to offshore sites after
               a few popular domestic sites are shut down. Our results have
               general implications for the governance of other illegal
               activities online. This paper was accepted by D. J. Wu,
