               (INFORMS)",
  volume    =  49,
  number    =  6,
  pages     = "801--815",
  abstract  = "The study presented in this paper examines how beliefs about
               coworkers affect group discussion and performance. Two beliefs
               are considered: (1) Perceptions of coworker task competence, and
               (2) achievement motivation. This study investigates whether these
               perceptions can actually hinder group discussion and performance,
               and considers the contexts in which these detrimental effects are
