               especially (but not only) in developing and transition economies.
               The model goes beyond the previously published studies in the way
               it describes the structure of bureaucratic “tracks,” and the
               information among the participants. Entrepreneurs apply, in
               sequence, to a “track” of two or more bureaucrats in a prescribed
               order for approval of their projects. Our first result
               establishes that in a one-shot situation no project ever gets
               approved. This result leads us to consider a repeated interaction
               setting. In that context we characterize in more detail the
               trigger-strategy equilibria that minimize the social loss due to
