  journal   = "European journal of political economy",
  publisher = "Elsevier BV",
  volume    =  27,
  number    =  4,
  pages     = "749--763",
  abstract  = "In this paper we measure perceptions of incorrect behavior or
               ‘small crime’, based on a questionnaire administered to a large
               representative sample from the Dutch population. In the
               questionnaire we ask the respondents to rate the severity or
               justifiability of a number of small crimes. We present short
               questions that only state the nature of the small crime, as well
               as vignette questions, describing in detail a fictitious person
               committing the small crime and other factors related to the
               circumstances in which the small crime is committed. We find that
               the perceived severity of small crimes varies systematically with
               characteristics of the respondent as well as of the person
