  number    =  5,
  pages     = "2357--2396",
  abstract  = "Virtually all theories of economic growth predict a positive
               relationship between population size and productivity. In this
               paper, I study a particular historical episode to provide direct
               evidence for the empirical relevance of such scale effects. In
               the aftermath of the Second World War, 8 million ethnic Germans
               were expelled from their domiciles in Eastern Europe and
