  journal   = "Games and economic behavior",
  publisher = "Elsevier BV",
  volume    =  87,
  pages     = "497--507",
  abstract  = "We consider a dynamic competition game involving three players,
               in which each player can vary the extent of his competition on a
               per-rival basis. We call such competition targeted. We show that
               if the players are myopic, then the weaker players eventually
               lose the game to their strongest rival. If instead the players
               are sufficiently far-sighted, then all three players converge in
               their power and stay in the game. We develop our model in
               application to drug wars, but the approach of targeted
               competition can be applied to competition between firms or
               political parties, or to warfare.",
