  volume    =  40,
  number    = "Part B",
  pages     = "387--390",
  abstract  = "Sometimes experimentalists draw far-reaching policy conclusions
               from their findings. However, this is dangerous if there is
               ambiguity with respect to the right interpretation of the
               results. A good example for this danger is the well-known study
               by Falk and Szech (Science, 2013), who conclude that “markets
               erode moral values”. If this were true, economists, who have
