               evidence by decision-makers in policing and crime reduction. The
               EMMIE framework was developed to meet this aim. It encapsulates
               five broad categories of research evidence that are considered
               relevant to crime reduction, namely Effect size, Mechanism,
               Moderator (or context), Implementation and Economics. In this
               paper, we chart the origins and development of EMMIE. We also
